{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus","id":925037,"title":"[2E] Ephemeral Beings - Too low Corpus?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-02T14:08:25-07:00","id":925037,"title":"[2E] Ephemeral Beings - Too low Corpus?","content":"Today I run <b>Mage</b> session about players confronting the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895970-\u200b-2e-mystery-yellow-sign-hallows-network-corruption-and-abyssal-astral-realm#post895970\">King in Yellow</a>, avatar of Goetic Abyssal Realm of <i>Carcosa</i>. Being it's avatar, it has max Rank of 5 - that means max Resistance is 15. Adding 5 from human-like Size and we have Corpus 20. My players in first turn get to do him 18 Aggravated damage - in the end they killed it just by one turn attacks.<br /> <br /> I know rules are made to let PCs to beat those things, but when comparing beings maxed stats to normal characters 7 Health box - it does not seems as low compared to using it on five experienced characters.<br /> <br /> I probably missed something - <b>Could you point me to Ephemeral Beings rules that made those god-like beings more resistant?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T14:57:05-07:00","id":925059,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea: Abyssals don't have to follow all the rules we are familiar with, even if we use Ephemeral stats for them. Consider borrowing the Dread Powers of the Idigam or bluebook Horrors. For example, the Colossus Dread Power of the Idigam gives General Armor equal to Resistance and 8 Again on melee attacks (Banes bypass this Armor). The King In Yellow doesn't have to be huge to borrow this power. Consider using custom Numina as well, such Amechra's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/278509-spooky-ghosts-and-nice-spirits-what-are-your-custom-numina\"><b>Awful Presence</b></a>.<br /> <br /> Also, do you remember the Fae Aspects of Gentry and hobgoblins in 1ED? You could do something similar and call them Abyssal Aspects to further customize your antagonist. Like, &quot;those who have seen the King In Yellow's play or read its plot suffer a X penalty to rolls for contesting its mind affecting powers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are supposed to be crazy, so go crazy too. Last tip: you can give melee weapons and Armor with ratings somehow based on Rank as free benefits that do not take up Numina slots. You could also temporarily boost those Weapons and Armor with Essence and/or Willpower points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-02-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:49:08-07:00","id":925135,"title":"","content":"This is the advice I gave Darinas the other day: if you have a big boss encounter, don't run it mechanically, run it thematically. Instead of asking how the mechanics handle it, ask how your narrative should handle it. What is the purpose of the encounter in the story? What should determine the outcome? What needs to happen before that? Storytellers are allowed to cheat, so just because the characters can toss enough aggravated to kill a character doesn't mean he's really dead.<br /> <br /> Determine some non-mechanical standard for your battles, like a number of turns or the resolution of a plot. I've had encounters where I've pre-determined a number of &quot;good hits&quot; my players need to make on an enemy. Once they do that, I just have the last one be the downing blow, then let them coup-de-gr\u00e2ce or capture the opponent, unless I decide it dies outright. Other times I have some sort of plot development going on which is resolved while they have a back and fourth with the villain. For instance, I plan to end the plot of my Dragon campaign with a bomb being dropped on the city while they fight a Deep One, and while 3 experienced Oroboroi with military backup can take down a Deep One, it's more about them actually resolving what's going on than going through the Deep One's 45 points of HP.<br /> <br /> Another really popular technique, which is mechanically supported and is even used heavily in modules, is to not allow them to defeat the big-bad through conventional means: make some specific thing the Occultists / Non-combat-characters have to do while the combat-oriented ones just smack him around. The last campaign I finished, the bad guy (who was basically a renegade Roman general) used some sort of blood bathing ritual to put a stone into his body which made him invincible, right before the battle, and we found out at the beginning of the battle that we needed to dip a sword in the blood he'd used in order to cut him. The battle ended with our army showing up after a few turns and basically holding him down and repeatedly whacking him with swords and maces as we took him somewhere else to do a few experiments before cutting the stone out of him. It wasn't about damage, because he was invincible, it was about overpowering him and utilizing information.<br /> <br /> This method is extremely useful for horror situations where the characters have been otherwise unable to fight the villain effectively. Look at <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/92564/Nightmare-on-Hill-Manor\" target=\"_blank\">Nightmare on Hill Manor</a> for an example, where the evil ghost causing the haunting is pretty much impervious to the characters, but is killed instantly by a counter-ritual.<br /> <br /> With the King in Yellow, I suggest you think about his powers, which involve being outside of space and time and influencing people by embedding himself in their minds. Don't have it be a simple act of tossing lightning bolts at him, have it be some crazy chase across several planes where they're trying to undo whatever you've decided he is.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Also, remember that the King is <i>clever</i>, they shouldn't be able to face him head-on, because he's expressly good at working from the shadows and avoiding direct confrontation. The real challenge shouldn't be getting through his health, it should be getting the chance to attack an otherwise weak opponent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-02-2016, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:50:51-07:00","id":925136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus#post925037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably missed something - <b>Could you point me to Ephemeral Beings rules that made those god-like beings more resistant?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You may have better luck if you put the entity in <i>any context other than multiple attackers throwing a collective truckload of aggravated damage at it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:39:12-07:00","id":925155,"title":"","content":"Seriously, I want to know how your players got 18 agg successes against someone I assume is supposed to be at least a story antagonist in one turn.I very rarely want math, but here it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T00:30:27-07:00","id":925248,"title":"","content":"I was suspecting King will not last longer than 3 turns with them, but not to be blast in one turn casting... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925155#post925155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, I want to know how your players got 18 agg successes against someone I assume is supposed to be at least a story antagonist in one turn.I very rarely want math, but here it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have cabal of Adepts and Masters of Arcana - <i>each</i> of six PCs can cast Aggraveted damage with Arcanum 4 spell with Reach, giving on start Arcanum dots in damage ( base Potency ). That means 6x4 Aggravated damage - two characters miss cast, so we only got 18 ( 2 Masters took -2 to roll to have even 5 Agg damage done ). As it's direct damage, it just pass through it.<br /> <br /> Not to mention they have with them group of <i><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/915818-2e-fan-choir-of-hashmallim\">Choir of Hashmalim</a> </i>members NPCs with them - 4 casters of Supernal Fire as Praxis...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-03-2016, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T00:43:53-07:00","id":925254,"title":"","content":"As to general problem with killing King in Yellow in this part of story - I do not have problem with that. He was <i>only</i> Royal Avatar of this entity that he represents ( Rank 6 ) - it's like killing one of Lunas bodies. Probably painful to god, irritating to him - but not big deal in the end. Especially as ego boost of 'gods slayers' lead them straight to the Carcosa Abyssal Realm itself... &lt;Evil ST grin&gt;<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, I want to make proper fight in Carcosa itself - King will be prepared on PCs on his home turf, locking them in his Abyssal Astral Realm.<br /> <br /> To easier maybe the rest of discussion, here are basic stats of Kings of Yellow Royal Avatar:<br /> <br /> <b>Name: </b>King in Yellow / Hastur<br /> <b>Type:</b> Abyssal Goetia<br /> <b>Rank: </b>5 ( Avatar of Rank 6 entity )<br /> <br /> <b>Power:</b> 15<br /> <b>Finesses:</b> 11<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> 13<br /> <br /> <b>Influances:</b> Madness 5<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> 5 to choose, thought about Posses<br /> <b>Numina: </b>11 to choose<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T00:51:29-07:00","id":925257,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10120_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10120\" data-vbnamecard=\"10120\">RockstarRaccoon</a> I like your advice - but it won't work in <b>Mage</b>. At certin level, PCs just can literally kill anything by thinking about it - all Arcana have 4th dot spell that let you make Aggravated damage to target. With &quot;Arcanum dots Potency as damage&quot; we look here on 4-5 Agg damage per turn, without sweating of character.<br /> <br /> @<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\">GibberingEloquence</a> good spot on's - but they do not work with concept of King in Yellow as entity. Colossal seems as much more appropriate to Dagon- like being, and would make fighting it impossible ( Resistance 13 Armor would mean that <i>non </i>of my PCs cabal and NPC could make damage to being ). <b>Aweful Presence</b> maybe interesting to use, but not solving our 'one shot problem'. Mundane equipment don't sound to work with <i>Avatar of Madness</i> beings concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-03-2016, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T06:09:46-07:00","id":925313,"title":"","content":"Don't expect Mage to play nice with combat scenarios lasting more than 1-2 turns. It's pretty badly balanced for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T06:38:40-07:00","id":925316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925248#post925248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was suspecting King will not last longer than 3 turns with them, but not to be blast in one turn casting... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We have cabal of Adepts and Masters of Arcana - <i>each</i> of six PCs can cast Aggraveted damage with Arcanum 4 spell with Reach, giving on start Arcanum dots in damage ( base Potency ). That means 6x4 Aggravated damage - two characters miss cast, so we only got 18 ( 2 Masters took -2 to roll to have even 5 Agg damage done ). As it's direct damage, it just pass through it.<br /> <br /> Not to mention they have with them group of <i><a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/915818-2e-fan-choir-of-hashmallim&quot;]Choir</a> of Hashmalim[/URL] </i>members NPCs with them - 4 casters of Supernal Fire as Praxis...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, they *reached* against the Avatar of a Godlike *Abyssal* entity? I'd have those attacks do nothing or even bolster it.<br /> <br /> Invoking Abyssal energies (via Paradox risk) against an Abyssal should be a logical no no.<br /> <br /> EDIT: or was this baseline casting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-03-2016, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T06:44:08-07:00","id":925317,"title":"","content":"They got Free Reach, probably. It's a chronicle with Gnosis 6 PC(s) with multiple Arcana at 4 and probably some at 5. <br /> Honestly, in your stead, I would start wrapping up the story for these particular characters and would restart at lower levels, or I would switch to non-standard plot challenges that don't get exploded by one salvo of Master spells. Or I would homerule certain things, like adding Withstand to damage and require certain levels of Potency to achieve stronger narrative effects.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:01:48-07:00","id":925321,"title":"","content":"Wait, it's Rank 6 and you gave it health boxes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:06:53-07:00","id":925323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925321#post925321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, it's Rank 6 and you gave it health boxes?</div> </div> </div> </div> No, it's a Royal Avatar of the Rank 6 entity. Royal Avatars are Rank 5, which is the maximum Rank where entities can be properly represented with stats instead of being plot devices.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10120_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10120\" data-vbnamecard=\"10120\">RockstarRaccoon</a> hit the nail on the head. I'm writing an Abyssal Aspect based on their advice right now and will post it soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:07:48-07:00","id":925324,"title":"","content":"Ah, gotcha, misunderstood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:19:40-07:00","id":925327,"title":"","content":"Other option to curb this specific issue: Numina/Dread Powers/whatever that<br /> - Allow the veing to roll Rank/Potency against incoming damage, either to downgrade or negate.<br /> - Aggravated (or any?) Damage sends the being into Totally-Not-Twilight for at least one round. This prevents multiple actors from piling damage up in a single round. <br /> <br /> If I were structuring this like a video game battle, I'd has more suggestions (but later - on my phone ATM).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:30:44-07:00","id":925329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925254#post925254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to general problem with killing King in Yellow in this part of story - I do not have problem with that. He was <i>only</i> Royal Avatar of this entity that he represents ( Rank 6 ) - it's like killing one of Lunas bodies. Probably painful to god, irritating to him - but not big deal in the end. Especially as ego boost of 'gods slayers' lead them straight to the Carcosa Abyssal Realm itself... &lt;Evil ST grin&gt;<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, I want to make proper fight in Carcosa itself - King will be prepared on PCs on his home turf, locking them in his Abyssal Astral Realm.<br /> <br /> To easier maybe the rest of discussion, here are basic stats of Kings of Yellow Royal Avatar:<br /> <br /> <b>Name: </b>King in Yellow / Hastur<br /> <b>Type:</b> Abyssal Goetia<br /> <b>Rank: </b>5 ( Avatar of Rank 6 entity )<br /> <br /> <b>Power:</b> 15<br /> <b>Finesses:</b> 11<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> 13<br /> <br /> <b>Influances:</b> Madness 5<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> 5 to choose, thought about Posses<br /> <b>Numina: </b>11 to choose<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just Mass Create Madness alone would guarantee the poor saps that didn't had Mind Shielding would end up trying to murder their cabalmates in such a fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:33:42-07:00","id":925330,"title":"","content":"So the sum up is that Corpus 20 is pinnacle for Royal Avatars to get by RAW, yes? I did not miss any rules? And there are not any powers to let Ephemeral Beings survive with some Armor on it? Because Colossal is too much on the other hand ( Armor 13 makes impossible to attack it, even for my PCs ).<br /> <br /> <b>Idea: </b>Maybe making Dread Power that rises Withstood based on Rank? It does not solve direct attack spells, but makes <i>very</i> problematic other magic.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>, if games must end at Gnosis 6 - or even Masters level, as the problem is more with spells itself - then what those stats are on sheet? Do you need to end game on Elders in <b>Vampire</b> or <b>Werewolf</b>? They are still non-Archmage characters, so there should be way to challenge them without breaking the system in all times. From looking in <b>CoD Rulebook</b> and <b>Mage</b> 2E I think it's the Storytelling System 2E lacking some higher power Dread Powers for combat oriented things. not that <b>Mage </b>system being simply too powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925329#post925329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just Mass Create Madness alone would guarantee the poor saps that didn't had Mind Shielding would end up trying to murder their cabalmates in such a fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not had chance - PCs got Initiative first... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, PCs make sure <i>everyone</i> have Mind Shield. They are mage payers of at least two years, in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-03-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:36:44-07:00","id":925332,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Abyssal Aspect:</b></i> Memetic<br /> <br /> The entity exists as a viral idea instead of a tangible and discreet construct, and knowing about it can be enough to infect someone. Abyssals possessing this Aspect gain the Aggressive Meme Numen for free, and can only use Manifestations besides Twilight Form after a certain set of prerequisites has been met. This usually takes the form of a ritual that, once complete, allows the entity to use all Manifestations. However, the prerequisites can also be a set of apparently disparate behaviors on part of the infected that gradually give more Manifestations to the entity.<br /> <br /> All entities who possess this Aspect spread through a vector, which must be present for the entity to use Aggressive Meme. A vector infects a number of roll types equal to the entity's Rank. An entity themed around mad art can affect Intelligence + Crafts rolls made to try and create a sculpture of its likeness. Anyone who saw this sculpture would roll Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance vs Finesse + Rank. Failure indicates the target is infected by the meme for a number of days equal to Rank, or weeks if the entity gets an Exceptional Success.<br /> <br /> Of note is that Memetic entities lack Corpus. They exist within minds most of the time, so they treat anyone who is infected as being Open. To contain a Memetic entity, one must subvert, destroy and/or eliminate knowledge of the vector. These entities' effective Corpus is measured by their Willpower points. Each contained episode of an Aggressive Meme use takes away 1 willpower point. For each point lost, the entity suffers a cummulative -1 penalty to all rolls. When they lose all Willpower points, the Open Condition is considered to be suppressed, but care must be taken to contain the vector so the meme does not spread again.<br /> <br /> Although they cannot Materialize of use Influences on physical structures until the prerequisites have been met, Memetic entities can influence the minds of the infected via Urging/Influences/Numina so they act as proxies, often to spread the meme and attack those who want to contain it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-03-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:48:09-07:00","id":925337,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> all nice and funny - but this Aspect just makes being Goetia entiety ( i.e. it's in your mind ). Problem is that PCs are in Astral Realms and doing all those fights in there - so Goetia are <i>physical</i> there, even this Memetic one will be. And, let's not forget that Mind magic can easily block Aggressive Meme - I literally used it this Numen from Pallid ( Rank 4 servant of King ) that infected PCs with Yellow Sign madness - sadly, it worked only for whole 50 seconds, till our Mastigos did not cure it and member of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/915818-2e-fan-choir-of-hashmallim\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> used power to take back Abyss created madness by Second Attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T08:00:23-07:00","id":925343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925337#post925337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> all nice and funny - but this Aspect just makes being Goetia entiety ( i.e. it's in your mind ). Problem is that PCs are in Astral Realms and doing all those fights in there - so Goetia are <i>physical</i> there, even this Memetic one will be. And, let's not forget that Mind magic can easily block Aggressive Meme - I literally used it this Numen from Pallid ( Rank 4 servant of King ) that infected PCs with Yellow Sign madness - sadly, it worked only for whole 50 seconds, till our Mastigos did not cure it and member of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/915818-2e-fan-choir-of-hashmallim\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> used power to take back Abyss created madness by Second Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure what the problem is. With that Aspect, the entity can be Materialized in multiple places simultaneously, so even if you &quot;kill&quot; it in one place, you still have to &quot;kill&quot; it in any other places where people have been infected (and that's just the Royal Avatar). Please remember that the PCs are being helped by specialists in fighting Abyssals.<br /> <br /> If the problem is that it's too easy to counter a Memetic entity's powers with Mind Arcanum, consider adding the following to the Aspect:<br /> <br /> On top of being strengthened by Paradox and Quiescence, Memetic entities are very hard to banish directly. The entity's Rank is doubled for the purposes of decreasing Potency, and it can spend 1 willpower point to further increase its Rank by 4 for one scene. A successful Fraying, Unraveling or Unmaking spell against the entity only removes 1 Willpower point, regardless of the leftover Potency.<br /> <br /> Does that help? Also, why did you say &quot;nice and funny&quot;?<br /> <br /> EDIT: And isn't the real fight supposed to take place in Carcosa?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-03-2016, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T08:02:06-07:00","id":925344,"title":"","content":"Bends the rules a bit, but what about Mass Creating other Madness Ephemeral entities? Like madness personified.<br /> <br /> And it's a &quot;Boss&quot; - always give it the first action, unless it leads to a TPK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T08:17:05-07:00","id":925351,"title":"","content":"Also, you could let these Memetic entities roll Resistance + Rank once per scene if the PCs did not contain the spread of the vector in the other locations. Each Success restores 1 willpower point, which would stack with what I suggested in my previous post. You could also give the King In Yellow the Versatile Energies Numen, so he can convert Essence, Corpus and Willpower into each other on a 1 for 1 ratio.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If the PCs can cause so much aggravated damage without incurring Paradox, perhaps you should take the focus away from combat and make maximum use of that Madness 5 Influence. Fool the PCs into focusing on things that are not real, so the physically stronger servants of the King can sneak up on them. Use as many illusions as you want at the same time, so the PCs do not have time to cast Mind spells on everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-03-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T08:44:46-07:00","id":925359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925248#post925248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was suspecting King will not last longer than 3 turns with them, but not to be blast in one turn casting... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We have cabal of Adepts and Masters of Arcana - <i>each</i> of six PCs can cast Aggraveted damage with Arcanum 4 spell with Reach, giving on start Arcanum dots in damage ( base Potency ). That means 6x4 Aggravated damage - two characters miss cast, so we only got 18 ( 2 Masters took -2 to roll to have even 5 Agg damage done ). As it's direct damage, it just pass through it.<br /> <br /> Not to mention they have with them group of <i><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/915818-2e-fan-choir-of-hashmallim\">Choir of Hashmalim</a> </i>members NPCs with them - 4 casters of Supernal Fire as Praxis...</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Did your Avatar try and approach them alone or with followers, hidden or otherwise? In a situation where all things are equal or did it try to put them in a time-place-perception that would slant things in it's favor? Was there anything that the avatar had in it's favor for this encounter? If it didn't have anything going for it, did it try to sneak or run away instead of engaging them?<br /> <br /> Because if not, then there's your problem. I don't care how badass your statted enemy is, if it's got stats, is going against a group of Adepts and Masters, and does nothing to tilt things in their favor, they are going to be torn apart every time. If the circumstances they are fighting in could be mistaken for a white room test, they're going to be torn apart. You have to challenge them sideways.<br /> <br /> You never, <i>ever</i> fight on a level playing field. You <i>always</i> have something up your sleeve. You <i>always</i> play unfairly against the PC's. They' should, after all, be playing unfairly against your NPC's, trying to wring every advantage they can against them.<br /> <br /> The other part of this is fudging in accordance to the story. If this thing wasn't supposed to die that easy, you cheat-I mean, come on, it's the avatar of a Rank 6 Abyssal Entity, if anything has cheat codes going on for it, it's this. Still, I know you have a thing for mechanical adherence, so we'll ignore that and go back to &quot;How did you stack the deck?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T08:56:50-07:00","id":925366,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> has some very good points. I mean, it's not a very interesting encounter if it boils down to &quot;kill the thing&quot;. Abyssals of this Rank should be capable of offering a bargain of some sort to convince the players to cooperate with it instead of just going in with guns blazing. In fact, the King should expect a violent entrance and have a plan B if the PCs don't want to make deals with an Abyssal. It could simply make shit up about the PCs to sow distrust among them. It could pretend to surrender and lead them to a trap. It could have trapped Sleeper witnesses to prevent the PCs from firing wildly.<br /> <br /> Combat for its own sake is only entertaining for so long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:13:22-07:00","id":925372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925343#post925343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sure what the problem is. With that Aspect, the entity can be Materialized in multiple places simultaneously, so even if you &quot;kill&quot; it in one place, you still have to &quot;kill&quot; it in any other places where people have been infected (and that's just the Royal Avatar). Please remember that the PCs are being helped by specialists in fighting Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, maybe I read Aspect wrong. If that means that King is many places at the same time ( like multiple clones of it ) it does have a much more sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925343#post925343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Of note is that Memetic entities lack Corpus. They exist within minds most of the time, so they treat anyone who is infected as being Open. To contain a Memetic entity, one must subvert, destroy and/or eliminate knowledge of the vector. These entities' effective Corpus is measured by their Willpower points. Each contained episode of an Aggressive Meme use takes away 1 willpower point. For each point lost, the entity suffers a cummulative -1 penalty to all rolls. When they lose all Willpower points, the Open Condition is considered to be suppressed, but care must be taken to contain the vector so the meme does not spread again.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>From my reading it states that there is one 'clone' of Memetic entity based on Willpower. That means there are up to 10 copies of it ( as Ephemeral Beings Willpower cannot be more than 10 ). Also, what vector will add to fighting it in Astral? If vector is only 'see the play', in Astral you cannot make it work without larger journey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925343#post925343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of being strengthened by Paradox and Quiescence, Memetic entities are very hard to banish directly. The entity's Rank is doubled for the purposes of decreasing Potency, and it can spend 1 willpower point to further increase its Rank by 4 for one scene. A successful Fraying, Unraveling or Unmaking spell against the entity only removes 1 Willpower point, regardless of the leftover Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does you mean by 'decreasing Potency'? <i>Mental Shield</i> spell just makes you roll Clash of Wills all the time against powers of any Goetia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925343#post925343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, why did you say &quot;nice and funny&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe used wrong English idiom - I thought that Aspect is cool to use in other games and examples, but I think it does not solve King in Yellow problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925343#post925343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: And isn't the real fight supposed to take place in Carcosa?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is. But Carcosa is Anima Mundi Abyssal Realm of Hyades Star Claster - so it's <i>still</i> is Astral space. And by this, any Goetic or Memetic entetiy still should be 'physical' there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925344#post925344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bends the rules a bit, but what about Mass Creating other Madness Ephemeral entities? Like madness personified.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was thinking about spamming the center battlefield with Pallid's and lower Madness Goetia. It just sound to me a bit cheap - and still do not solve the problem that Royal Avatars, by RAW, cannot have more Corpus than 20 - I can make Dagon-like Godzila that is unkillable with Colossal Dread Power, or let Avatar to have like 20 Corpus and just let PCs to puff it in one turn of casting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, if not got any other idea, will go with 'summon large Madness army' in Carcosa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925344#post925344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's a &quot;Boss&quot; - always give it the first action, unless it leads to a TPK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in a scene where Boss want's to trap players - he build their confidence, let them get into his turf. He was waiting for them to talk to him - but they just killed him. Well, now they are on his land - we will see how they will let his live...<br /> <br /> Also, if you got PCs with high Initiative, it's a bit cheating to make Boss 'always first'. Ephemerals have high Initiative from start -&gt; Finesses + Resistance, on they example I wrote is like 24. Still, PC or two can beat it with good rolls and Merits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925351#post925351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you could let these Memetic entities roll Resistance + Rank once per scene if the PCs did not contain the spread of the vector in the other locations. Each Success restores 1 willpower point, which would stack with what I suggested in my previous post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vector idea clashes with fight in Astral...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925351#post925351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also give the King In Yellow the Versatile Energies Numen, so he can convert Essence, Corpus and Willpower into each other on a 1 for 1 ratio.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting - Where is this Numen described in? If King will stand one turn of attack, he could regenerate his lost Corpus.<br /> <br /> Could he get <i>extra</i> Corpus somehow?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925351#post925351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the PCs can cause so much aggravated damage without incurring Paradox, perhaps you should take the focus away from combat and make maximum use of that Madness 5 Influence. Fool the PCs into focusing on things that are not real, so the physically stronger servants of the King can sneak up on them. Use as many illusions as you want at the same time, so the PCs do not have time to cast Mind spells on everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good advice - I did forget that Influences works also in sublim way. But did not using those hallucinations on PCs be contested by <i>Mind Shield</i> all the time? After first or two of those they will be arguing ( rightfully ) that they do not have benefit of spell they are cast on themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:34:11-07:00","id":925383,"title":"","content":"<b>Note: </b>I made sure that King in Yellow is not real problem of situation - he is, in reality, summoned by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy\">Children of the Stars</a> Scelesti in material world. PCs got hint of it by going throught the Children HQ Astral represtantation to Carcosa. So they will need to solve this thing. But for now they are in Astral and good story need a good physical confrontation, so we think here about this combat scenario.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> - It was a bit 'white room scenario', I admit. It was <i>plan</i> of King to let them kill it there. I was just astonished that powerfull Ephemerals do not have any resistances on magic by books, in general. And King is preparing fight for PCs in Carcosa, on his homeland. First fight was dry test - and we have a bit problem that cabal can easily obliterate Royal Avatars. Now let's find solution to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925366#post925366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals of this Rank should be capable of offering a bargain of some sort to convince the players to cooperate with it instead of just going in with guns blazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>WHAT can offer entetiy of madness to mages that made a squad of Awakaned to kill it and destroy it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925366#post925366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, the King should expect a violent entrance and have a plan B if the PCs don't want to make deals with an Abyssal. It could simply make shit up about the PCs to sow distrust among them. It could pretend to surrender and lead them to a trap. It could have trapped Sleeper witnesses to prevent the PCs from firing wildly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sleeper witness thing is interesting - we have comatos Mastigos PC sister that is Sleepwalker, but is known from being target of psychic attacks in past ( previously it were Seers of Throne ). Thought about using it for a few session - here maybe a good time for using here as backup. <br /> <br /> Still, it will end with PCs probably wanting to kill King quicker - <b>HOW to make a confrontation longer that one turn of Adepts and Masters spells?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925366#post925366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat for its own sake is only entertaining for so long.</div> </div> </div> </div>We did not have a good fight in long time, so it is time for it. Hoped that Ephemeral Beings rules could help in here without 'just use plot device'...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:39:00-07:00","id":925386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>: The Memetic Aspect can give as many clones of the King as you want. If neighborhood A and B have been infected, A could have 3 Kings and B could have 10. When you remove the vector from A, all 3 clones disapper, and 1 Willpower point is lost (the maximum of 10 willpower dots is still in effect).<br /> <br /> By decreasing Potency, I meant Withstanding. I forgot that was the term, sorry.<br /> <br /> The Versatile Energies Numen is from Summoners page 223.<br /> <br /> Ok, if you want the King to be simply harder to kill, here's another Abyssal Aspect:<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox Gorging:</b> The entity reflexively rolls Resistance + Rank whenever Paradox is incurred in its presence. Each Success heals 1 lethal or bashing damage, and 3 Successes heals 1 aggravated damage. Also, they double their Resistance to calculate their Corpus. They may use their Influence over Paradoxes in conjunction with this Aspect and Numina to keep healing every turn.<br /> <br /> Also, please remember that the King can use Influence Paradox 4 to FORCE Paradox upon a spell. If you want to make him really dangerous, give him Influence Paradox 5.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, let's say that <b>Paradox Gorging</b> let's an Abyssal reflixvely eat another of equal or lesser Rank by by spending 1 willpower point and rolling Power + Rank vs Resistance + Rank. Success destroys the target Abyssal, and the gorging entity heals [the target's Rank x 2] in any type of damage. With Influence Paradox 5, Manifestation Paradoxes will happen more often, allowing the King to feast on the lesser Abyssals, or sic them on the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-03-2016, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T16:46:01-07:00","id":925556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925383#post925383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> - It was a bit 'white room scenario', I admit. It was <i>plan</i> of King to let them kill it there. I was just astonished that powerfull Ephemerals do not have any resistances on magic by books, in general. And King is preparing fight for PCs in Carcosa, on his homeland. First fight was dry test - and we have a bit problem that cabal can easily obliterate Royal Avatars. Now let's find solution to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that makes sense(and it's one of the advantages to the Royal Avatars-they can come back).<br /> <br /> Question: You did remember to treat Rank as Withstand, yeah?(I forget, tangentially, if it is' Rank or Resistance, but it's one of the two)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T16:49:15-07:00","id":925558,"title":"","content":"They used Damage spells. Damage Spells don't interact with Withstand. Ephemeral use Rank for Withstand, but in this instance, it's irrelevant. If it was relevant, though, it would cut down the damage to near 0, if not 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:10:03-07:00","id":925569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925558#post925558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They used Damage spells. Damage Spells don't interact with Withstand. Ephemeral use Rank for Withstand, but in this instance, it's irrelevant. If it was relevant, though, it would cut down the damage to near 0, if not 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damage spells are Withstood by your Stamina, Resistance in this case-well, actually Rank since that seems to always be the case(Still haven't gotten to my PDF yet). You have to overcome that with Potency before anything happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:11:49-07:00","id":925571,"title":"","content":"That's not true in 2nd ED.<br /> EDIT<br /> <br /> Ok, I finished a boss fight in a game, so I can expand:<br /> Damage Spells (Fraying, Unraveling) are not Withstood. Some spells that do damage (example - Devouring the Slain) *do* have Withstand ratings, but their first and primary function isn't to be a Damage Spell. Not a single Damage Spell in the game has a Withstand rating, and we have been told that it's a deliberate choice, because target's Health Bar is &quot;equivalent of the Withstand score&quot; here. The logic here is that you need to accumulate more Potency in a single Damage Spell than target's Health to one shot it, so a Withstand score would be redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-03-2016, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:22:28-07:00","id":925576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925571#post925571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not true in 2nd ED.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I've discovered. Ignore me on that rant, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:23:31-07:00","id":925577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925569#post925569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damage spells are Withstood by your Stamina, Resistance in this case-well, actually Rank since that seems to always be the case(Still haven't gotten to my PDF yet). You have to overcome that with Potency before anything happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, specifically not. You already have a resistance against damage spells - your health boxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:25:18-07:00","id":925578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925577#post925577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, specifically not. You already have a resistance against damage spells - your health boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, as I discovered. I actually clicked on my pdf after posting that, and it was on the page where it says that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:28:20-07:00","id":925579,"title":"","content":"The reason why I object to that design choice is that while it's supposed to be Withstand equivalent, it doesn't act like Withstand equivalent. Other spells don't reduce victim's Withstand Rating by their Potency on a unsuccessful attempt, and you can't get multiple casters to stack their Potencies in order to beat a Withstand score in a single turn, like Wyrd's group did there.<br /> <br /> Wyrd, isn't one of them a pretty advanced Time Mage? Because the &quot;upgraded&quot; version of their strategy is to have Acceleration running on the whole group, so they always have initiative and always can do the Alpha Strike :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-03-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:30:21-07:00","id":925580,"title":"","content":"Well, mind you, Wyrd's Group is ridiculously overpowered for the scenario they were in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:36:37-07:00","id":925583,"title":"","content":"Yeah, which is why I think they ascended the combat level where damage and health bars matter, and should probably fight with - and against - world shattering Conditions and Tilts. <br /> The problem with Mage is that, though, you have a pretty finite amount of resources that you can use on pre-emptive defence and each instance of such defence can only cover a pretty limited angle of attack, while Mages have pretty much infinite possible angles of attack, especially on the higher end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:44:17-07:00","id":925587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925583#post925583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, which is why I think they ascended the combat level where damage and health bars matter, and should probably fight with - and against - world shattering Conditions and Tilts.<br /> The problem with Mage is that, though, you have a pretty finite amount of resources that you can use on pre-emptive defence and each instance of such defence can only cover a pretty limited angle of attack, while Mages have pretty much infinite possible angles of attack, especially on the higher end.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where that Half-Blood Prince mentality is very important, and it applies to Abyssal Beings and other high-tier ephemeral beings too.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For those who might not be aware of my reference, here ya go:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Prime Minister:</b> But for heaven's sake, you're <i>wizards</i>! You can do <i>magic</i>! Surely you can sort out... well... <i>anything!</i><br /> <b>Cornelius Fudge</b>: The trouble is, the other side can do magic too, Prime Minister.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:57:54-07:00","id":925593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925583#post925583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Mage is that, though, you have a pretty finite amount of resources that you can use on pre-emptive defence and each instance of such defence can only cover a pretty limited angle of attack, while Mages have pretty much infinite possible angles of attack, especially on the higher end.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book didn't really go into antagonists other than other Mages, as well.<br /> <br /> And actually most of Chronicles and World of Darkness books lack storyteller advice regarding building suitable threats and antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:41:00-07:00","id":925620,"title":"","content":"I mean, let's put it this way.<br /> <br /> You're putting an enemy up against a group of PCs that are <i>optimized</i> to face that kind of enemy... and you're surprised that they dusted the guy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T19:37:10-07:00","id":925639,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'll be honest, most of the time I think ephemeral beings are a touch on the overpowered side, and I would wager that your average PC group of 4-5 people from any given line other than maybe mage would have an extremely hard struggle against a rank 5 being with 20 Corpus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T19:44:28-07:00","id":925643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925639#post925639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'll be honest, most of the time I think ephemeral beings are a touch on the overpowered side, and I would wager that your average PC group of 4-5 people from any given line other than maybe mage would have an extremely hard struggle against a rank 5 being with 20 Corpus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even a group of Disciples would have a not-easy time with one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:13:09-07:00","id":925654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925639#post925639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'll be honest, most of the time I think ephemeral beings are a touch on the overpowered side, and I would wager that your average PC group of 4-5 people from any given line other than maybe mage would have an extremely hard struggle against a rank 5 being with 20 Corpus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the kind of foe entire Protectorates form around combating - and that's specifically when it has agents on it's beck and call. But on it's own? Half a dozen Uratha grappling it to death and sucking off all it's essence after crippling it? Not an unlikely scenario.<br /> <br /> It goes like a terrorist lone wolf getting tackled to the ground. Sure, it'll hurt somebody, but it's more likely than anything that he's gonna get his comeuppance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:16:17-07:00","id":925658,"title":"","content":"A large part of the problem is the players going straight to Aggravated damage, something you're generally only able to do to ephemerals with a bane or special power. It just so happens that Mages have easy access to special powers. Another group, starting off with Lethal, spirits reduce that to Bashing and you have a being with three times as much Corpus that can often heal itself, so something much more significant. But you start with Aggravated damage out the gate and they've got much less, especially when they're last in Initiative waiting for five people who are probably on to the idea that the big bad shouldn't get a chance to attack them.<br /> <br /> Storytellers should know the capabilities of the PCs and plan accordingly. If they <i>can </i>make a fight go quick and easy, prepare for them to do so.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> Yeah, one pack of 4-5 could probably do it, providing they had some combat-specced guys in it. Ironically, I think 20 is the Max Health for werewolves before Primal Urge 5. You would have to be a 'rocks fall, everybody dies' Storyteller to throw something like this against a coterie of vampires and forcing a fight, though. They aren't really made for ephemeral fighting. I imagine if they knew what was going on they would be the most likely to negotiate, next to Changelings. They would all be screwed if said ephemeral decided to fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-03-2016, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T22:34:32-07:00","id":925723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925658#post925658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would have to be a 'rocks fall, everybody dies' Storyteller to throw something like this against a coterie of vampires and forcing a fight, though. They aren't really made for ephemeral fighting. I imagine if they knew what was going on they would be the most likely to negotiate, next to Changelings. They would all be screwed if said ephemeral decided to fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, take into account that, as far as I know, the &quot;psychic&quot; Disciplines (Auspex, Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare, Obfuscate) still work on ephemerals. And everyone has access to at least one of those other than the Gangrel (Mekhet and Nos get two).<br /> <br /> But, yes - I'd have given The King in Yellow this:<br /> <br /> <b>Flesh of Paradox</b><br /> The ephemeral being is thoroughly tainted by the stuff of the Abyss - treat it as if it were an entire crowd of Sleepers for the purposes of calculating Paradox dice pools, except it adds dice equal to its Rank rather than just one. In addition, it may spend Essence reflexively to cancel Mana spent to mitigate a Paradox dice pool on a one-to-one basis.<br /> <br /> Boom - choke on 5 Paradox dice with 8-again and Rote that you have to burn <i>so much Mana</i> on to mitigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T23:07:30-07:00","id":925738,"title":"","content":"So we do not have official help on the subject \u2013 here is my fan answer. This Numina probably will need to be split in two for balance \u2013 If yes, then maybe you have appropriate name for Withstand part?<br /> <br /> <b>Resistant</b><br /> The entirety stubbornly sticks to life. It has general Armor equal to his Rank. More, she can decreases up to his Rank Aggravated damage to Bashing in each attack on it. Additionally, entity resist Supernal Magic much more efficiently than other of her kind \u2013 she get\u2019s automatic Withstand source equal to its Rank against mages magic. That means she generally have Rank+1 Withstand, as its Attributes are normal source of Withstand, as per rules of Withstanding, <b>MtAw</b> 2E page 114.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-04-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T23:22:07-07:00","id":925752,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> - I very like your Numina, will surly add them to King for 'spicing' things up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925386#post925386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, if you want the King to be simply harder to kill, here's another Abyssal Aspect:<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox Gorging:</b> The entity reflexively rolls Resistance + Rank whenever Paradox is incurred in its presence. Each Success heals 1 lethal or bashing damage, and 3 Successes heals 1 aggravated damage. Also, they double their Resistance to calculate their Corpus. They may use their Influence over Paradoxes in conjunction with this Aspect and Numina to keep healing every turn.<br /> <br /> Also, please remember that the King can use Influence Paradox 4 to FORCE Paradox upon a spell. If you want to make him really dangerous, give him Influence Paradox 5.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, let's say that <b>Paradox Gorging</b> let's an Abyssal reflixvely eat another of equal or lesser Rank by by spending 1 willpower point and rolling Power + Rank vs Resistance + Rank. Success destroys the target Abyssal, and the gorging entity heals [the target's Rank x 2] in any type of damage. With Influence Paradox 5, Manifestation Paradoxes will happen more often, allowing the King to feast on the lesser Abyssals, or sic them on the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would cut out double Resistant part to put it in the other Numina - Have any good name for it? - As shown in <b>CoD Rulebook</b> by <i>Stalwart </i>Numina, tricks with stats should be discrete parts of mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925723#post925723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Flesh of Paradox</b><br /> The ephemeral being is thoroughly tainted by the stuff of the Abyss - treat it as if it were an entire crowd of Sleepers for the purposes of calculating Paradox dice pools, except it adds dice equal to its Rank rather than just one. In addition, it may spend Essence reflexively to cancel Mana spent to mitigate a Paradox dice pool on a one-to-one basis.<br /> <br /> Boom - choke on 5 Paradox dice with 8-again and Rote that you have to burn <i>so much Mana</i> on to mitigate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would only switch names between Paradox Gorging and Flesh of Paradox - they named exactly as the <i>other</i> power works. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So <b>Gib</b>'s Numina would be called <i>Flesh of Paradox</i> and <b>amechra</b>'s <i>Paradox Gorging</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> - If you are okay with this, we could start Abyssal Numina topic in <b>Mage</b> subforum with your powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-04-2016, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T02:11:15-07:00","id":925799,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Sure, a thread for custom Abyssal powers sounds useful. Feel free to post my Memetic and Paradox Gorging Aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T03:27:11-07:00","id":925814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925738#post925738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More, she can decreases up to his Rank Aggravated damage to Bashing in each attack on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just say &quot;no, if your spell isn't exploiting one of the entity's Banes, then it isn't doing agg damage&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T03:52:44-07:00","id":925818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925814#post925814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just say &quot;no, if your spell isn't exploiting one of the entity's Banes, then it isn't doing agg damage&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite, ephemera is harder to lastingly harm than mere flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:46:31-07:00","id":925975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925799#post925799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Sure, a thread for custom Abyssal powers sounds useful. Feel free to post my Memetic and Paradox Gorging Aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Topic created <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/925972-2e-abyssal-aspects-and-numina\">here</a> - look for continuing discussion there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925814#post925814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just say &quot;no, if your spell isn't exploiting one of the entity's Banes, then it isn't doing agg damage&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But HOW can spell exploit Bane? Unless it's attack spell that 'summons silver cross' thing, any other attacks will be useless - it's overpowered in other extreme than now situation where mages can just spam Aggravated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925818#post925818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite, ephemera is harder to lastingly harm than mere flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you rephrase this? I do not understand this comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:13:27-07:00","id":926077,"title":"","content":"You want that Dread Power that reduces all damage that <i>isn't</i> inflicted by an Exceptional Success to one Bashing.<br /> <br /> Yes, this includes Aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T15:48:20-07:00","id":926114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=925975#post925975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But HOW can spell exploit Bane? Unless it's attack spell that 'summons silver cross' thing, any other attacks will be useless - it's overpowered in other extreme than now situation where mages can just spam Aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you see why Royal Avatars are not to be trifled with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But seriously, fighting entities on this level is all about preparation. Either you know their weakness(es), or you're royally screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T18:11:32-07:00","id":926193,"title":"","content":"If I wanted to spin it as a big throw down battle, I'd let the avatar of big H spawn incarnate Madness minions with it's influence, probably dip into something like those Abyssal Aspects, give it a numina to rendering it &quot;outside&quot; if it takes Aggravated damage, and flood the area with insane cultists. Tagging TKY with Aggravated forces it out of the battle for a bit (but it never takes more than one attack's worth of Aggravated at a time) so it doesn't contribute, but the Madness minions and Paradox aggravating cultist keep the Cabal occupied in the interim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T20:44:21-07:00","id":926234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926077#post926077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want that Dread Power that reduces all damage that <i>isn't</i> inflicted by an Exceptional Success to one Bashing.<br /> <br /> Yes, this includes Aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would be Unbreakable. It would go nicely with some Armor, so even if you do get an Exceptional Success on the attack, your full damage will be reduced.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T23:00:18-07:00","id":926285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926077#post926077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want that Dread Power that reduces all damage that <i>isn't</i> inflicted by an Exceptional Success to one Bashing.<br /> <br /> Yes, this includes Aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even from Legacy Attainments? ExcepSucs are not so wierd ones you got dicepools of 10-15 ( Gnosis 6 + Arcana 4-5 + Rote Mudra ) or Praxis on Celestial Fire. Still, making one Bashing is lesser than ( up to Rank ) Bashing I proposed before - and I'm <i>not sure it's good thing</i>. I thought about using 'Twice Resistance as Corpus' <b>Gib</b>'s proposition, so Bashing numbers are a bit secondary - and at least players will not make murder eyes on me by remaking their 'we can kill by one though power' ( 6 Aggs ) in to 'you barely scratch him' (1 Bash ).<br /> <br /> I think that balance of ( NPC Rank ) Bash damage is okay, more or less. / Like from 2-5 Bash, based on Rank / But then we have weird thing that higher Rank being is, the more Bashing it will get. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe something like (6 - Rank) Bashing? Then, yes, <i>King in Yellow</i> will get only 1 Bash per attack - but then Pallid ( Rank 4 ) will take 2 Bash, for example. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926234#post926234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That would be Unbreakable. It would go nicely with some Armor, so even if you do get an Exceptional Success on the attack, your full damage will be reduced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unbreakable is official power in some book? With ExcepSucs you still will be making those at least 4 Aggravated damage so unless Armor power will also reduce Aggravated on Rank basis...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926114#post926114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you see why Royal Avatars are not to be trifled with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But seriously, fighting entities on this level is all about preparation. Either you know their weakness(es), or you're royally screwed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to make this explicit combat situation - <i>not</i> killing players. Even then, Spirit and Mind mages just could cast &quot;I make it work like Bane&quot; spell. ( I would do that at this level on their place ). I looking for making bosses toughter, not unbeatable - if I would, I would just take Colossus power that was raised on previous power. 'Resistance as Armor' is more than enough to render beings not killable to anything than plot device at Rank 4-5. It's <b><i>not</i></b> my intention. I work for challange players, not just kill them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-05-2016, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T00:36:11-07:00","id":926309,"title":"","content":"Unbreakable is in CoD core; it <i>explicitly</i> drops the damage to 1B unless it's an Exceptional Success. Armor doesn't change that, since you have 1B of &quot;ping&quot; damage through armor regardless of how much you have.<br /> <br /> I mean, your real problem is that you gave the party a group of extra Mages <i>optimized</i> to murder abyssals. That's the equivalent of tossing the King's sheet into a woodchipper and wondering why it came out mangled.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> But <i>seriously</i> - why is Supernal magic even <i>effectual</i> against the King? It'd be <i>perfectly</i> legit to downgrade all damage from Supernal sources by one step. He should be dragging Carcosa with him <i>everywhere he goes</i>, mangling language into a recitation of <i>The King in Yellow</i> and separating everyone involved from the Supernal Realms.<br /> <br /> The place you were fighting the King? Counts as an abyssal verge.<br /> You were doing it in the Astral? Oh good, the local Ecstatic Winds are tainted, and flay Mana as easily as they do &quot;flesh&quot;.<br /> You won? Yay! Now you have to deal with the fact that <i>all</i> the local Goetia have been warped to fit Carcosa, and are <i>murderously</i> angry that you just killed their King.<br /> <br /> Hell, at the very least the King should have been using the Idigam rules + Abyssal Entity rules, not the Spirit rules + Abyssal Entity rules. <i>All</i> the Annunaki should be built that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T05:06:53-07:00","id":926364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926309#post926309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unbreakable is in CoD core; it <i>explicitly</i> drops the damage to 1B unless it's an Exceptional Success. Armor doesn't change that, since you have 1B of &quot;ping&quot; damage through armor regardless of how much you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed the Dread Powers section in <b>CoD</b> Rulebook - if this is official power, I just take this, with other Abyssal ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926309#post926309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <i>seriously</i> - why is Supernal magic even <i>effectual</i> against the King? It'd be <i>perfectly</i> legit to downgrade all damage from Supernal sources by one step.</div> </div> </div> </div>For spells - of course, it works and is logical. For Legacy-like powers... well, I think it can also be made<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926309#post926309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He should be dragging Carcosa with him <i>everywhere he goes</i>, mangling language into a recitation of <i>The King in Yellow</i> and separating everyone involved from the Supernal Realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I think about powers like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926309#post926309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The place you were fighting the King? Counts as an abyssal verge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Carcosa will sure works as one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926309#post926309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were doing it in the Astral? Oh good, the local Ecstatic Winds are tainted, and flay Mana as easily as they do &quot;flesh&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is wicked! I'm was thinking I will tweak Ecstatic Wind - thanks for particular idea on that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926309#post926309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You won? Yay! Now you have to deal with the fact that <i>all</i> the local Goetia have been warped to fit Carcosa, and are <i>murderously</i> angry that you just killed their King.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Carcosa - sure. In London where game is - will probably need to take a bit longer. Still, large squads of twisted Goetia are cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926309#post926309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, at the very least the King should have been using the Idigam rules + Abyssal Entity rules, not the Spirit rules + Abyssal Entity rules. <i>All</i> the Annunaki should be built that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, what's are differences between Idigam and Ephemeral rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T05:57:32-07:00","id":926369,"title":"","content":"Remember, if your Abyssal Entity is larger than size 5 (even just Size 6), all spells that don't increase their Scale factor appropriately will fail. <br /> Size also increases Corpus, so that's a plus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T06:24:38-07:00","id":926373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926369#post926369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, if your Abyssal Entity is larger than size 5 (even just Size 6), all spells that don't increase their Scale factor appropriately will fail.<br /> Size also increases Corpus, so that's a plus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know - only <i>King in Yellow</i> is human size ( by Chambers stories ). Still, nice thing to take into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title