us?p=926373#post926373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good to know - only <i>King in Yellow</i> is human size ( by Chambers stories ). Still, nice thing to take into consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Size 6 is the upper extreme of human size. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T07:56:20-07:00","id":926412,"title":"","content":"Also, Abyssal. Just because it <i>looks</i> human-sized doesn't mean it <i>is. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T08:03:27-07:00","id":926416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926412#post926412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Abyssal. Just because it <i>looks</i> human-sized doesn't mean it <i>is. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'm big on the inside.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T09:16:39-07:00","id":926453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926416#post926416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I'm big on the inside.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And I can't think of any class of being that's more appropriate for than an Annunaki, avatar or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T09:54:17-07:00","id":926466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=926364#post926364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, what's are differences between Idigam and Ephemeral rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Formless Idigam have no Influences and bleed essence twice as fast as other spirits, but their Ban and Bane change every scene, all have a Dread Power called Shifting, and can use Essence Shaping powers on themselves. Coalesced Idigam have normal Essence Bleed, Influences, and a fixed Ban and Bane, can use Essence Shaping powers on anyone, and gain even more Dread Powers. There's a list of example Essence Shaping and Dread Powers in Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:16:46-07:00","id":926482,"title":"","content":"Also all Idigam have an essence pool twice as large as a spirit their rank should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T21:08:05-07:00","id":960214,"title":"","content":"Okay, as day of confrontation with King in Yellow is nearing, I\u2019m preparing the session. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As I want to make it most engaging and challenging to players, any idea will be helping.<b> Bonus points for engaging our Moros Arrow Matter Master, as it will be probably his players last game session with a team</b>. Some needed noble sacrifice can be good twist ending for him. Also, we should somehow split team to make those <i>Choir of Hashmallim</i> members \u2018get lost\u2019, so confrontation with King in Yellow would be much more memorable.<br /> <br /> What we have to this day:<br /> <b>Intro</b> \u2013 PCs entered Astral Carcosa ( Anima Mundi Abyssal Verge in Hyades Star ), where they ended on ruins of ancient civilization. Just past them, portal has closed and there are trapped in domain of <i>King in Yellow</i>\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>General Note</b> \u2013 Carcosa counts as Abyssal Verge ( \u20132 penalty to Skill rolls that depend on a knowledge of natural laws. Abyssal Verges provide +2 dice to Gnosis rolls to invite Paradox into a spell the way Scelesti do \u2013 Still, nothing about <i>automatic</i> higher Paradox for everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Ecstatic Wind in this foul domain is killing both Astral body and Mana in travelers ( but need to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960197-2e-astral-ecstatic-wind\">understand rules for Wind first</a> to make ruling on those ).<br /> <br /> Scenes:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Maze</b> \u2013 Carcosa is \u2018deserted\u2019 city that has no end and begging. Or rather it has, but King in Yellow is wrapping every ones senses. To get in real way someone need to use Magic \u2013 but how this should works? Simple Knowing spells of Space or Matter should work? We also want to split party somehow.</li> <li>???</li> <li><b>King in Yellow</b> \u2013 Final confrontation with Royal Avatar of Madness. To this day we have those stats of his:</li> </ol><b>Name: </b>King in Yellow / Hastur<br /> <b>Type:</b> Abyssal Goetia<br /> <b>Rank: </b>5 ( Avatar of Rank 6 entity )<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5 ( See <b>Flesh of Abyss</b> Numina why I left it lower )<br /> <br /> <b>Power:</b> 15<br /> <b>Finesses:</b> 11<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> 13<br /> <br /> <b>Influances:</b> Madness 5, Paradox 5<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> 5 to choose, thought about Posses<br /> <b>Numina: </b>11 to choose<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Unbreakable</b></li> </ol>The creature is nearly indestructible. Any attack that does not score an exceptional success inflicts only a single point of bashing damage. Exceptional successes inflict damage as normal. If the creature has a weakness of some sort, attacks incorporating that weakness bypass this power.<ul><li><b>Resistant </b>by me</li> </ul>Entity resist Supernal Magic much more efficiently than other of her kind \u2013 she get\u2019s automatic Withstand source equal to its Rank against Awakened spells. That means she generally have Rank+1 Withstand, as its Attributes are normal source of Withstand, see rules of Withstanding, <b>MtAw</b> 2E page 114.<ul><li><b>Flesh of Abyss</b> by me ( idea from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a> )</li> </ul>Entity is build from the stuff of Abyss itself. That means, Supernal Magic have really harder time to interact with it. Each spell cast on entity is treated as one Spell Factor lower \u2013 that means that attack spells makes one damage lower, Scale is treated as needing to get Size 6 to work on it at all and Duration is shorter than caster imagined when making Imago.<ul><li><b>Copies</b> by me</li> </ul>The entity is \u2018one in many\u2019. She can make copies of herself, working like effects of <i>Manifold Presence</i> spell, giving many possible instances of it. They all are connected to proper entity, but not so hurting. Each copy can be destroyed with full Bashing damage of Corpus from main entity and takes one Willpower from entity pool. Each copy is treated as entity itself for using it\u2019s powers or targeting it\u2019s targets.<ul><li><b>Paradox Gorging</b> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\">GibberingEloquence</a></li> </ul>The entity reflexively rolls Resistance + Rank whenever Paradox is incurred in its presence. Each Success heals 1 lethal or bashing damage, and 3 Successes heals 1 aggravated damage. They may use their Influence over Paradoxes in conjunction with this Aspect and Numina to keep healing every turn. Paradox Gorging let's an Abyssal reflexively eat another of equal or lesser Rank by spending 1 willpower point and rolling Power + Rank vs Resistance + Rank. Success destroys the target Abyssal, and the gorging entity heals [the target's Rank x 2] in any type of damage.<ul><li><b>Presence of Paradox</b> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a></li> </ul>The ephemeral being is thoroughly tainted by the stuff of the Abyss - treat it as if it were an entire crowd of Sleepers for the purposes of calculating Paradox dice pools, except it adds dice equal to its Rank rather than just one. In addition, it may spend Essence reflexively to cancel Mana spent to mitigate a Paradox dice pool on a one-to-one basis.<br /> And we still have next 5 Numina to choose for King\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Run </b>\u2013 To return to Earth, PCs need to somehow open the portal. But how can someone? \u2018Killing\u2019 King in Yellow? Best would be some kind sacrifice on Arrows behalf. Maybe there is needed to be spilled blood of humans to return to Earths realm? Or just classical \u2018we open portal, but someone need to stop them from getting us\u2019 as Arrow need to stay behind?</li> </ol><b>Problem is that PCs have 4 NPCs from Choir with them</b>. Still, possibility on \u2018noble ending\u2019 I think it\u2019s okay here. Someone need to be sacrificed \u2013 it can be Arrow, if player will have guts for this closing of his PCs line. Previous idea here: \u2018Now you have to deal with the fact that <i>all</i> the local Goetia have been warped to fit Carcosa, and are <i>murderously</i> angry that you just killed their King.\u2019","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-30-2016, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T05:22:52-07:00","id":960373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=960214#post960214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, as day of confrontation with King in Yellow is nearing, I\u2019m preparing the session. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As I want to make it most engaging and challenging to players, any idea will be helping.<b> Bonus points for engaging our Moros Arrow Matter Master, as it will be probably his players last game session with a team</b>. Some needed noble sacrifice can be good twist ending for him. Also, we should somehow split team to make those <i>Choir of Hashmallim</i> members \u2018get lost\u2019, so confrontation with King in Yellow would be much more memorable.<br /> <br /> What we have to this day:<br /> <b>Intro</b> \u2013 PCs entered Astral Carcosa ( Anima Mundi Abyssal Verge in Hyades Star ), where they ended on ruins of ancient civilization. Just past them, portal has closed and there are trapped in domain of <i>King in Yellow</i>\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>General Note</b> \u2013 Carcosa counts as Abyssal Verge ( \u20132 penalty to Skill rolls that depend on a knowledge of natural laws. Abyssal Verges provide +2 dice to Gnosis rolls to invite Paradox into a spell the way Scelesti do \u2013 Still, nothing about <i>automatic</i> higher Paradox for everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Ecstatic Wind in this foul domain is killing both Astral body and Mana in travelers ( but need to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960197-2e-astral-ecstatic-wind\">understand rules for Wind first</a> to make ruling on those ).<br /> <br /> Scenes:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Maze</b> \u2013 Carcosa is \u2018deserted\u2019 city that has no end and begging. Or rather it has, but King in Yellow is wrapping every ones senses. To get in real way someone need to use Magic \u2013 but how this should works? Simple Knowing spells of Space or Matter should work? We also want to split party somehow.</li> <li>???</li> <li><b>King in Yellow</b> \u2013 Final confrontation with Royal Avatar of Madness. To this day we have those stats of his:</li> </ol><b>Name: </b>King in Yellow / Hastur<br /> <b>Type:</b> Abyssal Goetia<br /> <b>Rank: </b>5 ( Avatar of Rank 6 entity )<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5 ( See <b>Flesh of Abyss</b> Numina why I left it lower )<br /> <br /> <b>Power:</b> 15<br /> <b>Finesses:</b> 11<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> 13<br /> <br /> <b>Influances:</b> Madness 5, Paradox 5<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> 5 to choose, thought about Posses<br /> <b>Numina: </b>11 to choose<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Unbreakable</b></li> </ol>The creature is nearly indestructible. Any attack that does not score an exceptional success inflicts only a single point of bashing damage. Exceptional successes inflict damage as normal. If the creature has a weakness of some sort, attacks incorporating that weakness bypass this power.<ul><li><b>Resistant </b>by me</li> </ul>Entity resist Supernal Magic much more efficiently than other of her kind \u2013 she get\u2019s automatic Withstand source equal to its Rank against Awakened spells. That means she generally have Rank+1 Withstand, as its Attributes are normal source of Withstand, see rules of Withstanding, <b>MtAw</b> 2E page 114.<ul><li><b>Flesh of Abyss</b> by me ( idea from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a> )</li> </ul>Entity is build from the stuff of Abyss itself. That means, Supernal Magic have really harder time to interact with it. Each spell cast on entity is treated as one Spell Factor lower \u2013 that means that attack spells makes one damage lower, Scale is treated as needing to get Size 6 to work on it at all and Duration is shorter than caster imagined when making Imago.<ul><li><b>Copies</b> by me</li> </ul>The entity is \u2018one in many\u2019. She can make copies of herself, working like effects of <i>Manifold Presence</i> spell, giving many possible instances of it. They all are connected to proper entity, but not so hurting. Each copy can be destroyed with full Bashing damage of Corpus from main entity and takes one Willpower from entity pool. Each copy is treated as entity itself for using it\u2019s powers or targeting it\u2019s targets.<ul><li><b>Paradox Gorging</b> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\">GibberingEloquence</a></li> </ul>The entity reflexively rolls Resistance + Rank whenever Paradox is incurred in its presence. Each Success heals 1 lethal or bashing damage, and 3 Successes heals 1 aggravated damage. They may use their Influence over Paradoxes in conjunction with this Aspect and Numina to keep healing every turn. Paradox Gorging let's an Abyssal reflexively eat another of equal or lesser Rank by spending 1 willpower point and rolling Power + Rank vs Resistance + Rank. Success destroys the target Abyssal, and the gorging entity heals [the target's Rank x 2] in any type of damage.<ul><li><b>Presence of Paradox</b> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a></li> </ul>The ephemeral being is thoroughly tainted by the stuff of the Abyss - treat it as if it were an entire crowd of Sleepers for the purposes of calculating Paradox dice pools, except it adds dice equal to its Rank rather than just one. In addition, it may spend Essence reflexively to cancel Mana spent to mitigate a Paradox dice pool on a one-to-one basis.<br /> And we still have next 5 Numina to choose for King\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Run </b>\u2013 To return to Earth, PCs need to somehow open the portal. But how can someone? \u2018Killing\u2019 King in Yellow? Best would be some kind sacrifice on Arrows behalf. Maybe there is needed to be spilled blood of humans to return to Earths realm? Or just classical \u2018we open portal, but someone need to stop them from getting us\u2019 as Arrow need to stay behind?</li> </ol><b>Problem is that PCs have 4 NPCs from Choir with them</b>. Still, possibility on \u2018noble ending\u2019 I think it\u2019s okay here. Someone need to be sacrificed \u2013 it can be Arrow, if player will have guts for this closing of his PCs line. Previous idea here: \u2018Now you have to deal with the fact that <i>all</i> the local Goetia have been warped to fit Carcosa, and are <i>murderously</i> angry that you just killed their King.\u2019</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure how vulnerable they might be to it, but if you are splitting the party, maybe The King could try striking deals with individual members out of earshot. If the players are up for it, you could take each of them aside in turn and give them your tempting deal. Then each would know the others got the same deal, but don't know their answers. Who is really an ally?<br /> <br /> Another option is to play up hallucinations and madness, and see if you can get the characters to fight each other (but think they are attacking other minions of Hastur). Turn their own strengths against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}